# Boxplots for HILIC Batch 2 - DCIS vs. IDC (normalized, log, scaled data)

A summary of the various metabolites can be found in the excel file "DCIS_IDC_Meta_analysis_CS.xlsx". In this Excel file, there are separate tabs for analysis of HILIC Batch 1 and 2 and ICMS Batch 1 and 2. There are also tabs for meta analysis between the 2 batches for both HILIC and ICMS. The DCIS.CCR2high and DCIS.CCR2low groups are combined to a DCIS group, increasing the n from 3 to 6 for the DCIS group.  

Meta analysis of DCIS vs IDC between Batch 1 and 2 is in word file "DCIS_IDC_Meta_analysis_CS.docx". Meta analysis of DCIS High vs DCIS Low between Batch 1 and 2 is in word file "DCIS_High_v_Low_Meta_analysis_CS.docx".  

Total of 475 metabolites.

```{r readdata1, echo=FALSE}

load(file ="W:/Health Services and Outcomes Research/BEC/Brooke Fridley/consult/Cheng.Nikki/R01 DCIS/data/processed_data/HILIC_processed_new_data.Rdata")

hilic.B2.meta <- read_excel("W:/Health Services and Outcomes Research/BCB/members/Sakitis.Chase/Consult/Cheng.Nikki/Chase_Results/DCIS_IDC_Meta_analysis_CS.xlsx",
                            sheet = "HILIC.Batch.2")

data.trans.hilic.B2<-HILICdata

n.metabolites.hilic.B2<-ncol(data.trans.hilic.B2)-2

data.trans.hilic.B2 <- data.trans.hilic.B2 |> filter(Group != "Normal")
data.trans.hilic.B2$Group <- str_replace(data.trans.hilic.B2$Group,"DCIS.CCR2high","DCIS")
data.trans.hilic.B2$Group <- str_replace(data.trans.hilic.B2$Group,"DCIS.CCR2low","DCIS")


```


